From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Belousov <michael.belousov98@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:15:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] web: custom fragment programs in the draw stream

A backend can compile a fragment shader of its own (wasm_programCreate) and draw parts
of a stream through it: a -3 step switches to it, with its vec4 uniforms (uData) from
the stream's uniform buffer and up to two more textures at units 1 and 2 (uTex1,
uTex2). It runs on dvui's own vertex shader and vertex layout, so dvui's geometry
feeds it unchanged. A source is written against a short prelude that builds it as
GLSL ES 3.00 or 1.00 (VARYING, TEX, FRAG_COLOR, MAX_VEC4); one starting #version is
taken as it is, on WebGL2 only.

Programs link while frames go on where the context has KHR_parallel_shader_compile;
wasm_programStatus says when one is ready. wasm_programMaxVec4 says how many uniform
vec4s a program may use, asked of the context once. A punch blend (dst * (1 - src.a))
joins the texture blends for a program to cut out what it covers.
---
 src/backends/web.js | 181 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 175 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/web.js b/src/backends/web.js
index afc813b..cecf29a 100644
--- a/src/backends/web.js
+++ b/src/backends/web.js
@@ -203,16 +203,27 @@ export class Dvui {
     /// `undefined` is unknown, and sends it.
     gls = {};
     /// One framebuffer per render-target texture, attached once (texture id -> framebuffer):
     /// re-attaching a texture to the one shared framebuffer on every switch made the driver
     /// check the framebuffer again each time.
     targetFramebuffers = new Map();
     /// The matrix uniform's storage, filled in place.
     matrix = new Float32Array(16);
+    /// Custom programs (`wasm_programCreate`), by id: `{ prog, loc, status, mw, mh, mfb }`.
+    /// Id 0 is dvui's own (`stock`). The program draws go through is `cur`; each keeps its own
+    /// matrix as last set, since a uniform belongs to its program.
+    programs = new Map();
+    stock = null;
+    cur = null;
+    newProgramId = 1;
+    /// KHR_parallel_shader_compile, where there is one: a program compiles while frames go on.
+    parallelCompile = null;
+    /// The most uniform vec4s a program may have, asked of the context once.
+    programMaxVec4 = undefined;
 
     // The modifier bits dvui reads (web_mod_code_to_dvui), from any keyboard or mouse event.
     modCode(ev) {
         return (ev.metaKey << 3) + (ev.altKey << 2) + (ev.ctrlKey << 1) + (ev.shiftKey << 0);
     }
 
